course: dictionary
lesson: 5579
title: One word, many levels
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word «level» has several meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. «I reached level 5 of the game» means a stage in a game. «Park on level 2» means a floor of a building. Read the words next to the word to find the clue.
explain: «The water level rose as the boat went up the lock.» Here level means a height or amount. Ask yourself: what is going up or down? If it is a height, level means a height or amount.
explain: Level can also be an adjective, meaning flat and even. «A bike helmet sits snug and level, just above the eyebrows» means the helmet is straight across the head, not tilted. Try your meaning in the sentence: does flat and even make sense? Then you have it.
fact: A level can be a height or amount, a stage in a game, or a floor of a building.
fact: As an adjective, level means flat and even, with no part higher than another.
fact: «Sea level» is the height of the sea, and it is used to measure mountains: «Mount Everest is the highest mountain above sea level at 8,849 metres.»
fact: «Level best» means your very best, as in «I did my level best».
fact: To level something means to make it flat.
exercise: «I reached level 5 of the game.» What does level mean here? | A height above the sea | A floor of a building | A flat, even surface | *A stage in a game
exercise: «Park on level 2.» What does level mean here? | *A floor of a building | A height of water | To make something flat | Equal in score
exercise: «Make sure the shelf is level before you put the books on.» What does level mean here? | A stage in a game | *Flat and even, with no part higher than another | A floor of a building | The same score as someone else
test: «The match ended level at two goals each.» What does level mean here? | *Equal in score | Flat and even | A floor of a building | A stage in a game
test: «Use a spirit level to check the shelf is flat.» What is a spirit level used for? | Counting the steps up to a floor | *Checking that something is flat | Measuring the depth of the sea | Measuring how fast a car goes
exam: Ben says, «I did my level best on the test.» What does he mean? | He got the lowest mark in the class | He sat on the second floor | He made the paper flat on the desk | *He tried as hard as he could
